["3d","augmented-reality","canvas","html5","javascript","svg","virtual-reality","webaudio","webgl","webgl2","webgpu","webxr"],"visibility":"public","forks":36156,"open_issues":609,"watchers":109825,"default_branch":"dev","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mrdoob/three.js/pulls/20444","html_url":"https://github.com/mrdoob/three.js/pull/20444","diff_url":"https://github.com/mrdoob/three.js/pull/20444.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/mrdoob/three.js/pull/20444.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"**Description**\r\n\r\n<del>Uses `sizeInMult4 = byteLength + ( 4 - byteLength & 3 )`</del> **Updates 2025**: The formula should be simply...\r\n\r\n```js\r\nsizeInMult4 = byteLength + /*extra bytes count*/( -byteLength & 3 ) \r\n```\r\n\r\n... which **derives extra byte count from remainder** by leveraging 2's complement of the `byteLength` two LSBs ...:\r\n\r\nbyteLength | 2's complement & 3 \r\n-------------|------------------------\r\n0bxxxx_xx00  (4n+0)|  0bxxxx_x100 & 3 = 0 \r\n0bxxxx_xx01  (4n+1)|  0bxxxx_xx11 & 3 = 3 \r\n0bxxxx_xx10  (4n+2)|  0bxxxx_xx10 & 3 = 2 \r\n0bxxxx_xx11  (4n+3)|  0bxxxx_xx01 & 3 = 1 \r\n\r\n... the numbers are exactly the extra bytes count we needed. \r\n\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mrdoob/three.js/issues/20444/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mrdoob/three.js/issues/20444/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"}]